  /* --- the console ------------------------------------------------------- */

  /* One object, not six panels.
     Six cards of identical radius, fill and shadow read as a form; the eye has
     nothing to fix on and no idea what the subject is. So the head, the sheet
     picker, the stage, the altimeter, the readout and the buttons are all one
     instrument with hairlines between its parts, and the only other thing on
     the page is one line of text below it.

     Nothing sits directly on the sky. That was true when the panels were pale
     and it is still true now they are dark: the backdrop passes through every
     luminance there is on the way up, and no single text colour survives that.
     Every word is on the console, and check-fold-scene.mjs holds the console
     to 4.5:1 at every fold. */
  .console {
